1
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:04,480
弗里曼：时间
Time.

2
00:00:04,590 --> 00:00:06,890
与我们形影相随
It's all around us.

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:09,970
然而它是我们所以为的那样么？
But is it what we think it is?

4
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:14,360
时间的流逝仿佛一直向前…
Time seems to flow forward...

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,300
…然而它能够倒流么？
...But can it run backward?

6
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:22,210
事件的发展是此起彼伏的么
Do events unfold one after another,

7
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:26,550
还是过去 现在和将来并存的呢？
or do past,present,and future exist side-by-side?

8
00:00:26,660 --> 00:00:30,050
它是科学上最具挑战的课题之一
It's one of the most challenging topics in science,

9
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:34,730
质疑着我们对现实最基本的假设
questioning our most basic assumptions about reality.

10
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:39,870
时间是宇宙最基本的组成部分
Is time a fundamental part of the Universe,

11
00:00:39,980 --> 00:00:42,780
抑或有可能时间并不是真的存在呢？
or could it be that time doesn't really exist?

12
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:52,250
科学频道 - 穿越虫洞 2x03
Science.Channel - Through the Wormhole 2x03

13
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:57,370
空间 时间 生命本身
Space,time,life itself.

14
00:00:59,610 --> 00:01:04,510
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

15
00:01:08,890 --> 00:01:15,090
时间真的存在么?
Does Time Really Exist?

16
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:20,310
时间为何物？
What time is it?

17
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:23,780
我可以告诉你此时是晚上9：02分
I could tell you it's 9:02 p.m.,

18
00:01:23,890 --> 00:01:25,650
然而你的时间可能会有所不同
but your time may vary,

19
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:28,650
这取决于你身处何时何地
depending on where and when you are.

20
00:01:28,770 --> 00:01:30,850
对于我们大多数人来说
For most of us,

21
00:01:30,970 --> 00:01:34,520
时间就是我们用来度量我们日子的一组数字
time was a set of numbers we use to gauge our days.

22
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:37,190
我们过日子靠时钟——
We live our lives by the clock --

23
00:01:37,310 --> 00:01:41,560
起床 上班 睡觉 周而复始
waking up,racing to work,going to bed,and on and on.

24
00:01:41,680 --> 00:01:43,980
并不总是这样
It wasn't always like that.

25
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:49,710
我小时候 夏季遥遥无期
When I was a kid,summers were timeless.

26
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:52,810
我没有特定的地方要去
I had no particular place to be,

27
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:55,810
无所事事
no appointments to be kept.

28
00:01:55,930 --> 00:02:00,950
我的日子只被太阳的位置所限定
My days were bounded only by the position of the sun.

29
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:04,090
时间在当年无关紧要
Time didn't matter so much back then.

30
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:09,060
现在我的生活是一场与时间的赛跑
Now my life is a race against time.

31
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:12,100
然而我在与什么争分夺秒呢？
But what am I racing against?

32
00:02:12,210 --> 00:02:15,900
时间真是宇宙不可分割的东西么？
Is time a real thing built into the universe?

33
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:18,540
或者它只是一个抽象的东西
Or is it just an abstraction,

34
00:02:18,650 --> 00:02:20,170
是我们人类所创造的
something we humans created

35
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,140
保持我们文明不断前进的东西呢？
to keep our civilizations running?

36
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:24,470
为求答案
For the answer,

37
00:02:24,590 --> 00:02:28,810
我们得提出一个看似简单的问题——
we have to ask a deceptively simple question --

38
00:02:28,930 --> 00:02:31,410
时间为何物？
what is time?

39
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:34,420
想想吧 努力去定义它吧
Think about it. Try to define it.

40
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:36,490
谈何容易
It's not easy.

41
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:39,490
时间 它维系着突然冒出来的一切东西
Time is what keeps everything from happening all at once,

42
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,630
所以时间构成了世界
and so time is that part of the world

43
00:02:41,740 --> 00:02:43,800
以某种方式安排着事件
that orders events in a certain way

44
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:48,310
它们相继发生 从头到尾
so they happen sequentially,from beginning to end.

45
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:49,450
[ 窃笑 ]
O(∩_∩)O~Chuckles

46
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:53,000
我们在神经科学里所认识到的是
What we're realizing in neuroscience

47
00:02:53,450 --> 00:02:56,310
时间并不是我们认为的那样
is that time is not what we thought it was.

48
00:02:56,420 --> 00:03:00,850
时间并不是你被动跟着走的东西
Time is not something you're passively tracking.

49
00:03:00,960 --> 00:03:02,650
相反 它是
Instead,it's something

50
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:05,480
你用大脑主动构建的东西
that you're actively constructing with the brain.

51
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,520
我的大脑和你的大脑在如何看待
And my brain and your brain can be very different

52
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:11,090
同样的事件上会有很大的差异
in terms of how they see the same event.

53
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:13,930
时间并不存在
Time just does not exist.

54
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:15,430
所存在的只是
What exists is

55
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:18,200
世上一切东西的这些分配
these distributions of everything in the world,

56
00:03:18,310 --> 00:03:19,960
这些东西我称其为“nows”
these what I call "nows."

57
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,380
那是实实在在的东西
That's the real thing.

58
00:03:23,210 --> 00:03:26,380
我所喜欢的是时间是它的记录
What I enjoy about time is the recording of it.

59
00:03:28,090 --> 00:03:30,680
弗里曼：对于罗杰.史密斯 时间就是金钱
To Roger Smith,time is money.

60
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:32,610
他的定制手表要卖到
His custom-made watches sell

61
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:35,880
几十万美元
for hundreds of thousands of dollars.

62
00:03:35,990 --> 00:03:38,350
这活计最难得部分就在于
The hardest part of the job is

63
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:42,460
让这一大堆小齿轮 舵轮
to get these jungles of tiny gears and wheels ticking

64
00:03:42,570 --> 00:03:44,330
走出精准的间隔
at precisely spaced intervals.

65
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:47,860
为了拿出一块计时用表
To bring a watch to time,

66
00:03:47,970 --> 00:03:51,230
那可是一个漫长而复杂的过程
it can be quite a lengthy and complex process,

67
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:54,670
这个特殊的舵轮得精准地平衡
and this particular wheel has to be perfectly balanced.

68
00:03:54,780 --> 00:03:57,170
如果它不是精准平衡
And if it isn't perfectly balanced,

69
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:00,870
那么你的表将在不同的状态下
then your watch will keep different rates,

70
00:04:00,990 --> 00:04:02,640
走出不同的速度 不同的时间
different times in different positions.

71
00:04:02,750 --> 00:04:04,440
弗里曼：罗杰的目标是
Roger's goal is

72
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:07,910
让他的表来匹敌格林威治标准时
to get his watches to match Greenwich Mean Time,

73
00:04:08,030 --> 00:04:10,480
那可是全世界所有时钟都用来
the time that every clock around the world uses

74
00:04:10,600 --> 00:04:12,430
作为基准的时间
as its baseline.

75
00:04:14,270 --> 00:04:17,160
其名字来自这个地方 -
It was named after this place --

76
00:04:17,270 --> 00:04:19,560
英国格林威治
Greenwich,England.

77
00:04:19,670 --> 00:04:22,760
时间 我们知道它诞生于此地
Time as we know it was born here.

78
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:24,330
1884年
In 1884,

79
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:28,100
世界大会决定子午线
a world conference decided that the Meridian Line

80
00:04:28,210 --> 00:04:31,300
穿过格林威治天文台
that passes through the observatory at Greenwich

81
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:33,940
作为本初子午线 -
was to be the initial meridian --

82
00:04:34,050 --> 00:04:36,710
行星地球的母时
the master time for planet Earth.

83
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:40,650
格林威治时间是我们最接近
Greenwich Mean Time is our best approximation of time

84
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:43,210
艾萨克.牛顿爵士所描述的时间 -
as described by sir Isaac Newton --

85
00:04:43,330 --> 00:04:45,450
一个恒定节拍
a steady beat pounding

86
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:48,090
隐藏在宇宙背景里
behind the scenes of the Universe.

87
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:51,860
牛顿相信宇宙就像是一面大时钟
Newton believed the Universe was like a giant clock

88
00:04:51,970 --> 00:04:54,490
其推手是上帝
set into motion by God.

89
00:04:54,610 --> 00:04:57,310
但牛顿错了
But Newton got it wrong.

90
00:04:59,710 --> 00:05:02,030
李.斯莫林是位理论物理学家
Lee Smolin is a theoretical physicist

91
00:05:02,150 --> 00:05:05,070
试图解开时间之谜
trying to solve the mysteries of time.

92
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:07,910
牛顿的时间概念就是它是绝对的
Newton's concept of time was that it was absolute.

93
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:11,210
它就像是节拍器 这个 如你所说
It was like a metronome,which,as you said,

94
00:05:11,320 --> 00:05:13,180
滴答个不停 从不考虑
ticks on absolutely,without regard

95
00:05:13,290 --> 00:05:16,080
宇宙间是否发生了什么
to whether anything is happening in the Universe or not,

96
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,580
即使啥都没发生
even if nothing is happening.

97
00:05:17,690 --> 00:05:19,880
比如 即使在我们这个录音棚里
For example,even if in our studio here,

98
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,350
没有音乐演奏
no music is playing,

99
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:25,190
节拍器只是一股脑地以同样的速度滴答作响
the metronome just kicks on absolutely at the same rate,

100
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:27,490
无论发生什么事
no matter what is going on.

101
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:32,300
这里的问题是实际上我们所有人
The problem with this is that it's actually impossible

102
00:05:32,410 --> 00:05:34,730
都不可能发现绝对时间的
for any of us to detect absolute time.

103
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:37,330
我们发现不了绝对时间
We don't detect absolute time.

104
00:05:37,450 --> 00:05:40,500
我们发现时间是作为所发生的事情之间的关系
We detect time as relationships between things that happen,

105
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:41,940
我们可以来阐述一下
and we can illustrate this

106
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,320
请音乐家来响起音乐
by asking the musicians to start up the music.

107
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:47,250
1,2,3,4
One,two,three,four.

108
00:05:55,130 --> 00:05:57,350
他们开始演奏
And they start to play,

109
00:05:57,470 --> 00:06:00,020
他们在展开他们自己的时间
and they develop time between themselves,

110
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:02,320
相关的时间完全建立在
a relational time completely built

111
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:04,330
他们所演奏的音符之间的关系
from the relationships between the notes they're playing,

112
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,930
他们正在打创造的事件
the events they're creating.

113
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:08,100
那就是时间的真实模样
That's what time is really like.

114
00:06:08,210 --> 00:06:10,470
所以 我们可以将节拍器关闭
So,we can turn the metronome off.

115
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:13,170
事实上 我们可以甩掉它
In fact,we can just get rid of it,

116
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:14,940
世界没停下来
and the world keeps going on,

117
00:06:15,050 --> 00:06:18,720
音乐在进行 和之前一样
the music keeps going on just as before.

118
00:06:22,890 --> 00:06:25,050
这就是爱因斯坦的伟大见解
This was the great insight of Einstein,

119
00:06:25,160 --> 00:06:27,680
这就是他的广义相对论的基础 -
and it was the basis of his general Theory of Relativity --

120
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:30,450
时间的产生来自于
that time is created by the relationships

121
00:06:30,570 --> 00:06:32,990
宇宙中发生的变化关系
of the changes that happen in the Universe,

122
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:34,940
仅此而已
and nothing else.

123
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:44,570
弗里曼：即使在今天
Even today,

124
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,570
有些人还是很难接受
some people have a hard time accepting

125
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:49,140
艾伯特.爱因斯坦的相对时间
Albert Einstein's relational time

126
00:06:49,250 --> 00:06:51,810
超过艾萨克.牛顿的绝对时间
over Isaac Newton's absolute time.

127
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:54,640
不过我们得到的报时越好
But the better we get at telling time,

128
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:58,820
我们就越能看到爱因斯坦的正确
the more we can see that Einstein was right.

129
00:06:58,930 --> 00:07:02,690
这是台铝离子实验时钟
This is the aluminum ion experimental clock

130
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:05,990
国家标准与技术研究院里
at the National Institute of Standards and Technology

131
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,690
位于科罗拉多州的博尔德
in Boulder,Colorado,

132
00:07:07,810 --> 00:07:10,860
那是美国官方计时器
America's official timekeepers.

133
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:13,500
它是世界上最精确的时钟
It's the world's most accurate clock,

134
00:07:13,610 --> 00:07:16,640
测量超冷原子的震荡
measuring the oscillations of supercooled atoms.

135
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:17,870
其保持时间
It keeps time

136
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:23,210
误差在37亿年1秒之内
to within one second every 3.7 billion years.

137
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:27,010
2010年 博尔德的时间领主
In 2010,Boulder's time lords

138
00:07:27,130 --> 00:07:32,890
将两台离子钟并排放在一起精准同步
took two ion clocks side by side in perfect synchronization,

139
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:37,530
然后将其中一台钟抬高12英寸
then moved one of the clocks up 12 inches.

140
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,960
抬高的钟失去了同步
The higher clock went out of sync.

141
00:07:40,070 --> 00:07:44,400
其节拍比较低的钟稍稍快了一点点
It beat just a tiny bit faster than the lower clock,

142
00:07:44,510 --> 00:07:47,940
因为较高的钟只是稍稍远离了
because the higher clock is just a tiny bit farther away

143
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:50,810
地球引力的牵引
from the gravitational pull of the Earth,

144
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,810
这减缓了物体的下降
which slows things down.

145
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:56,180
爱因斯坦早在20世纪初
Einstein predicted this would happen

146
00:07:56,290 --> 00:07:58,880
就预言过这种情况
back at the dawn of the 20th century,

147
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,500
他只是开了个头
and he was just getting started.

148
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:08,260
如果我们感觉的宇宙如爱因斯坦所描绘的那样
If we perceived the Universe as Einstein pictured it,

149
00:08:08,370 --> 00:08:12,010
生活就必定不会是平滑线性的进程
life would not have to flow in a smooth,linear progression.

150
00:08:16,510 --> 00:08:19,000
一个简单的行为可以切开重新排列
A simple act could be cut up and rearranged

151
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:23,240
并无前后的逻辑方向
with no logical direction backward or forward,

152
00:08:23,350 --> 00:08:25,740
并无始末
no beginning or end.

153
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:27,750
这就会是宇宙的模样
This is how the Universe would look

154
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:31,460
若是我们完全失去时间的话
if we were physically unstuck in time.

155
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:36,550
肖恩.卡罗尔是一位物理学家
Sean Carroll is a physicist

156
00:08:36,670 --> 00:08:40,290
任职于加州理工学院
at the California Institute of Technology.

157
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:41,530
我们生活在空间里
We live in space.

158
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:44,300
我们的周围是一个三维的空间
All around us,there are three dimensions of space.

159
00:08:44,410 --> 00:08:47,430
爱因斯坦意识到时间也是个维度
What Einstein realized is that time is also a dimension.

160
00:08:47,550 --> 00:08:51,340
事实上 时间与空间是一回事 称为时空
In fact,time and space are one thing called space-time,

161
00:08:51,450 --> 00:08:52,870
那是四维的
which is four-dimensional.

162
00:08:52,980 --> 00:08:54,170
那就是我们所在之处
That's what we live in.

163
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:56,370
那就是我们在其中活动 生活的地方
That's what we move in and live our lives through.

164
00:08:56,490 --> 00:08:58,440
爱因斯坦进一步认识到
Einstein furthermore realized

165
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:03,050
引力是时空弯曲的一个表现
that gravity is a manifestation of the curvature of space-time.

166
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:04,620
你看宇宙间的东西——
You have stuff in the Universe --

167
00:09:04,730 --> 00:09:06,090
行星 黑洞
you know,a planet or a black hole

168
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:08,420
或某种物质 能量 -
or some kind of mass or energy --

169
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:10,720
弯曲了其周围的时空
it warps the space and time around it,

170
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:13,630
那就是我们所见到的引力
and that's what we see as gravity.

171
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:16,500
那实际上是弯曲了的时空
And it really is the space-time that gets warped.

172
00:09:16,610 --> 00:09:18,130
有时间 还有空间
It's time as well as space.

173
00:09:18,250 --> 00:09:21,600
因此 你若是走近一个强引力场
So,if you travel close to a strong gravitational field,

174
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:25,970
你就会感到时间的流逝不同于在外太空里
you feel the flow of time differently than in outer space.

175
00:09:26,090 --> 00:09:31,410
弗里曼：时间的相对性带来了好多奇怪的现象
The relativity of time causes a lot of strange effects,

176
00:09:31,530 --> 00:09:33,520
诸如对宇航员来说更快
such as time running faster for astronauts

177
00:09:33,630 --> 00:09:35,520
超过地球上的人
than people on Earth.

178
00:09:35,630 --> 00:09:38,720
然而爱因斯坦的时间之谜解决方案
But Einstein's solution to the mystery of time

179
00:09:38,830 --> 00:09:42,290
开辟了一个更具挑战的概念
opens up an even more challenging notion.

180
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:44,060
如果我们环顾四周
If we look around,

181
00:09:44,170 --> 00:09:49,430
我们会看到整个空间的存在就在此时此地
we see that all of space exists right here,right now.

182
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:52,800
那么 是不是随之 整个时间 -
So,doesn't it follow that all of time --

183
00:09:52,910 --> 00:09:56,940
过去 现在 将来 - 同样也已经存在了呢？
past,present,and future -- already exists,as well?

184
00:09:57,050 --> 00:10:02,010
难道说未来已经在这里了？
Could it be that the future is already here?

185
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,980
物理学称所有的时间段
Physics says that all the moments of time

186
00:10:04,090 --> 00:10:05,580
同样是真实的
are equally real,

187
00:10:05,690 --> 00:10:07,580
那就诱使我们宣称
and that tempts us into saying

188
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:09,890
它们同时存在着
that they all exist simultaneously,

189
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,090
它们现在都存在 但事实并非如此
they all exist now,but that's not what it's like.

190
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:14,620
不同的时间段
Different moments of time

191
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:16,260
其实就像空间中不同地方
are really like different places in space.

192
00:10:16,370 --> 00:10:17,390
它们不在这里
They're not here.

193
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:19,330
它们存在 但它们是在别处
They exist,but they're somewhere else.

194
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:21,360
不同之处在于 它不同于空间
The difference is that,unlike space,

195
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:23,770
我们经历时间只能
we can't help but experience time

196
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:25,870
一段接着一段
one moment after the other.

197
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:28,840
我们不能回到过去的时间段
We can't go back to moments in the past,

198
00:10:28,950 --> 00:10:33,210
我们不能在眼下和未来的时间段对话
and we can't,right now,talk to moments in the future.

199
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:36,440
弗里曼：此种时间错位
This sort of temporal dislocation

200
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:41,030
似乎有悖于物理定律和人类的经验
seems to contradict the laws of physics and human experience.

201
00:10:42,530 --> 00:10:44,000
会是这样么？
Or does it?

202
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:47,260
或许不是
Maybe not.

203
00:10:47,370 --> 00:10:48,790
此人会说
This man would argue

204
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:52,990
世界充满了迷失时间的人
that the world is filled with people who are unstuck in time

205
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:58,180
时间本身或许全在我们的头脑里
and that time itself may be all in our heads.

206
00:11:05,170 --> 00:11:09,930
时间真是隐藏在宇宙间的恒定节拍么？
Is time the steady beat behind the Universe?

207
00:11:10,310 --> 00:11:12,630
还是时间的改变
Or is time something that changes

208
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:16,100
就是因地而异 因人而异呢？
from place to place and person to person?

209
00:11:16,210 --> 00:11:17,500
我们年纪越大
The older we get,

210
00:11:17,620 --> 00:11:21,470
貌似伴我们前行的时光就越是匆匆
the faster the currents of time seem to carry us along.

211
00:11:21,590 --> 00:11:26,860
我们与时间的关系随着年龄而变化
Our relationship to time changes as we age.

212
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:33,290
研究表明时光的推移
Studies show that the passage of time

213
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:36,590
貌似随你的年纪的平方根而加快
seems to increase by the square root of your age.

214
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:39,160
所以 如在10岁时 它就是1:1
So,if at 10 years old,it's 1:1,

215
00:11:39,270 --> 00:11:43,000
当你到20岁时 它就是1:1.4
when you're 20,it's 1:1.4.

216
00:11:43,110 --> 00:11:47,340
而到你60岁时 它就是1:2.44了
And by the time you're 60,it's 1:2.44,

217
00:11:47,450 --> 00:11:50,600
快近2.5倍
about 2.5 times faster.

218
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:54,070
我们经历时间全都是1秒就是1秒
We all experience time at one second per second,

219
00:11:54,190 --> 00:11:56,240
然而并非感觉都是那样的
but it doesn't feel that way.

220
00:11:56,360 --> 00:11:59,580
贝勒医学院的大卫.依格曼
David Eagleman of the Baylor College of Medicine

221
00:11:59,690 --> 00:12:01,510
将其大半职业生涯打发在
has spent much of his career

222
00:12:01,630 --> 00:12:04,580
思索人类是如何感知时间的
puzzling out how humans perceive time.

223
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:07,590
他发现我们感知时间
He's found that our perception of time

224
00:12:07,700 --> 00:12:11,530
是受到生理和心理状态所支配的
is governed by biological and psychological states.

225
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:14,500
许多人在他们的闹钟尚未响起就醒来了
Many people will wake up just before their alarm clock,

226
00:12:14,610 --> 00:12:16,770
因为他们体内的昼夜节律
because as their body's circadian rhythm

227
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,740
一直在运转
is moving along,

228
00:12:18,850 --> 00:12:20,720
他们体内的信号告诉他们…
the signals in their body tell them...

229
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:24,210
…到起床的时候了 于是他们一跃而起
...This is the time to wake up,and then they pop awake.

230
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:27,240
弗里曼：我们得时间感也能被某些情况所改变
Our time sense can also be altered

231
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:29,980
如感觉到丧失
by things such as sensory deprivation,

232
00:12:30,090 --> 00:12:31,750
过度兴奋
overstimulation,

233
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:34,750
改变意识状态
and altered states of consciousness.

234
00:12:34,860 --> 00:12:37,490
因此 比如 人们吸食大麻时
So,for example,when people smoke marijuana,

235
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:41,220
他们有时会觉得 哇 我一直就站在这里没动过
they sometimes feel like,"Wow,I've been standing here forever."

236
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:42,530
我在这里有多久了？
How long have I been here?"

237
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:45,560
仿佛他们的时间流逝得很慢
And it's as though their passage of time is going slowly,

238
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:48,200
然而缓慢的时间感觉并不准确
but it's not exactly about slow time perception.

239
00:12:48,310 --> 00:12:52,200
我相信他们抵达那里时
I believe it's about their inability to nail down a memory,

240
00:12:52,310 --> 00:12:54,440
无力钉下一个记忆 一个记号
a landmark of when they arrived there.

241
00:12:54,550 --> 00:12:55,910
没有了那个记号
And without that landmark,

242
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:58,990
其感觉就像他们在那里好长时间了
it feels like they've been there for a very long time.

243
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:03,710
弗里曼：如果你曾遭遇过意外
If you've ever been in an accident,

244
00:13:03,830 --> 00:13:06,380
你就有可能经历奇怪的感觉
you might have experienced the strange feeling

245
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:08,490
整个事件宛如慢动作播放
that the whole event was playing in slow motion.

246
00:13:08,600 --> 00:13:11,620
然而不同于麻醉迷糊
But unlike a narcotic haze,

247
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:15,190
你还事无巨细记得一切
you recall everything in vivid detail.

248
00:13:15,310 --> 00:13:19,160
这是又一个记忆扭曲时间的例子
This is another case of memory warping time.

249
00:13:19,280 --> 00:13:21,730
在一个真正的高强度事件期间发生的是
What happens during a really high-intensity event is

250
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:25,940
你的大脑里有一个紧急控制中心
you have an emergency control center in your brain

251
00:13:26,050 --> 00:13:27,540
挂在了档上
that kicks into gear

252
00:13:27,650 --> 00:13:31,470
储藏了该事件过程非常密集的回忆
and lays down very dense memories during that event.

253
00:13:31,590 --> 00:13:34,410
所以 它好像是必定有很长一段时间
So,it seems like it must have taken a long time.

254
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:36,680
弗里曼：在任何特定的时刻
At any given moment,

255
00:13:36,790 --> 00:13:38,820
大脑都处理和同步
the brain processes and synchronizes

256
00:13:38,930 --> 00:13:42,090
大量的信息
an enormous amount of information.

257
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:44,320
简单动作实际上是小小的奇迹
Simple acts are actually small miracles

258
00:13:44,430 --> 00:13:47,120
是思想的速度和力量
of the mind's speed and power.

259
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:49,930
你打响指时 貌似同时发生的
When you snap your fingers,it looks like it's simultaneous.

260
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:51,790
貌似看到 听到的
It looks like the sight and the sound

261
00:13:51,910 --> 00:13:53,260
发生在同一时间
are happening at the same time.

262
00:13:53,370 --> 00:13:55,710
然而事实上 情况是…
But in fact,what's happening is...

263
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:59,300
…你的听觉系统能够通过耳朵
...Your auditory system is able to take information

264
00:13:59,410 --> 00:14:02,470
采集到信息 其过程很快
coming in through the ears and process that very quickly,

265
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:04,520
而你的视觉系统则要慢多了
whereas your visual system is much slower.

266
00:14:06,490 --> 00:14:09,510
因此 结果就是你的大脑听到了声音
So,what happens is your brain hears the sound,

267
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:11,210
然后看到了情景
and then it sees the sight,

268
00:14:11,330 --> 00:14:14,380
它得设法获得这两者
and somehow it has to take both of those

269
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:16,660
撮合在一起 端上来了…
and stitch them together and serve up...

270
00:14:18,070 --> 00:14:19,890
…一个故事 这就是它们同时发生
...A single story,which is that they were simultaneous,

271
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,390
即使信号传达给大脑
even though the signals are arriving at the brain

272
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:23,160
并非同时
at different times.

273
00:14:23,270 --> 00:14:25,530
这整个事情其实在时间上有点模糊
This whole thing is really smeared out in time,

274
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:27,900
然而我们并没有感觉到那样
and yet it doesn't feel that way to us.

275
00:14:28,010 --> 00:14:30,070
感觉仿佛是整个事情是同时发生的
It feels as though the whole thing is simultaneous.

276
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:32,970
弗里曼：用了百万分之几秒的时间
It takes a few millionths of a second

277
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,810
让你的大脑来拼凑信息
for your brain to put together information

278
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:37,780
将其提供给你的意识
and serve it up to your consciousness,

279
00:14:37,890 --> 00:14:42,610
这意味着我们都生活在那么一点点的过去
which means that we're all living a tiny bit in the past.

280
00:14:42,730 --> 00:14:46,420
这种时间滞后是我们大脑做出的权衡
This time delay is the tradeoff our brains make

281
00:14:46,530 --> 00:14:50,250
给我们最佳故事结果
to give us the best story of what happened.

282
00:14:50,370 --> 00:14:53,330
然而一旦大脑没有恰好得到故事
But when the brain doesn't get the story right,

283
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:56,030
你就会改变与时间的关系
it can change your relationship with time.

284
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:59,570
你的个人时间变得与众不同
Your personal time becomes different from others',

285
00:14:59,680 --> 00:15:02,970
那就可能产生极坏的后果
and that can have very bad consequences.

286
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:06,040
医学杂志说过奇怪的案件
Medical journals tell of the strange case

287
00:15:06,150 --> 00:15:08,410
有开车人
of the man who went for a drive

288
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:11,610
注意到路旁的树木和建筑飞驰而过
and noticed that the trees and buildings by the road

289
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:12,810
仿佛
were speeding by

290
00:15:12,930 --> 00:15:16,380
他开的车达到了时速200英里
as if he were driving at 200 miles per hour.

291
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:18,920
他松开油门
He eased up on the accelerator,

292
00:15:19,030 --> 00:15:22,160
但街景依然疾驰而过
but the cityscape continued to whiz by.

293
00:15:22,270 --> 00:15:26,430
此人感到世界在加速不停
This man perceived the world as having accelerated.

294
00:15:26,540 --> 00:15:29,900
在现实中 他已经放缓了
In reality,he had slowed down.

295
00:15:30,010 --> 00:15:32,970
他走路说话是慢动作
He walked and talked in slow motion.

296
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:37,370
他已经跟不上时间了
He had become unstuck in time.

297
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:40,110
原来 他的时间病的肇因
It turned out that his time sickness

298
00:15:40,220 --> 00:15:43,210
是脑肿瘤
was caused by a brain tumor.

299
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:48,280
不管时间是什么 它都与我们息息相关
Whatever time is,it's deeply wired into us.

300
00:15:48,390 --> 00:15:54,120
我们全都是具有自己内部时间的计时器
We are all clocks with our own internal time.

301
00:15:54,230 --> 00:15:55,620
大卫.依格曼怀疑
David Eagleman suspects

302
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:59,090
即使是稍与时间流逝不同步
that going even slightly out of sync with the flow of time

303
00:15:59,210 --> 00:16:02,900
都会导致严重的精神疾病
can lead to serious mental illness.

304
00:16:03,010 --> 00:16:05,130
我认为精神分裂症有可能根本上就是
I think that schizophrenia might fundamentally be

305
00:16:05,250 --> 00:16:07,130
时间感知紊乱
a disorder of time perception.

306
00:16:07,250 --> 00:16:10,640
所以试想你的时间感知上若有一些差异的话
So,imagine if there were some deficit in your time perception

307
00:16:10,750 --> 00:16:13,710
那你在有感知结果的前后
where you didn't know if your own actions were coming

308
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:16,910
就不会知道自己打哪里来的
before or after the sensory consequences.

309
00:16:17,020 --> 00:16:18,180
其结果就会是
What would happen is

310
00:16:18,290 --> 00:16:20,780
你会得到非常破碎的认知
you would have a very fragmented cognition.

311
00:16:20,890 --> 00:16:22,380
你不会知道哪些事情是你造成的
You wouldn't know which things you caused

312
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:23,860
哪些事情你不会造成的
and which things you didn't cause.

313
00:16:25,930 --> 00:16:28,760
弗里曼：为了表明我们得个人时间可以有多灵活
To show how flexible our personal time can be,

314
00:16:28,870 --> 00:16:31,290
大卫设计了一个实验
David devised an experiment

315
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:35,870
巧妙地扭曲测试对象的时间感知
that subtly warps a test subject's perception of time.

316
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:41,600
依格曼：这里 设想我看到你按下按钮
So,imagine that I have you press a button

317
00:16:41,710 --> 00:16:43,710
会产生一道闪光
and that causes a flash of light.

318
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:50,140
现在我注入很小的延迟
Now I inject a very small delay,

319
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:53,480
这样当你按下按钮时 闪光会出现
so that when you hit the button,the flash of light comes,

320
00:16:53,590 --> 00:16:56,620
比方说十分之一秒的滞后
let's say,1/10 of a second later.

321
00:16:56,730 --> 00:16:59,490
其结果就是你的大脑得习惯那种延迟
What happens is your brain gets used to that delay.

322
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,560
它开始了解到 当它产生这种行为时
It starts understanding that when it puts out this act,

323
00:17:02,670 --> 00:17:05,860
感知的反馈要略比预料的慢一点点
the sensory feedback is a little bit slower than it expected.

324
00:17:05,970 --> 00:17:07,760
开始调节它
So,it starts adjusting to that,

325
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:10,730
它就好像开始与你同步了
and it starts to seem simultaneous to you.

326
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:13,900
现在 如果我去除延迟 -
Now,if I remove the delay --

327
00:17:14,010 --> 00:17:16,440
现在你点击按钮 闪光立刻闪现 -
so now you hit the button and the flash happens immediately --

328
00:17:16,550 --> 00:17:17,800
你会相信
you will believe

329
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:21,450
闪光闪现时 你尚未按下按钮
that the flash happened before you pressed the button.

330
00:17:23,520 --> 00:17:26,180
这正是精神分裂症所发生的情况
This is exactly what happens in schizophrenia.

331
00:17:26,290 --> 00:17:28,720
有人会做出一个举动 称 “这不是我”
Somebody will make an act and say,"It wasn't me."

332
00:17:28,830 --> 00:17:32,490
我并不觉得我就是做那举动的人
I don't feel like I was the one who caused that."

333
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:36,160
弗里曼：时间貌似因人而异
Time seems to vary from person to person,

334
00:17:36,270 --> 00:17:39,430
我们主观时间的弹性
and the elastic nature of our subjective time

335
00:17:39,540 --> 00:17:43,760
已经让大卫怀疑时间是否真的存在
has caused David to wonder whether time is,in fact,real.

336
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:46,770
依格曼：我认为时间有可能是
I think that time might be

337
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:50,370
我们所具有的最顽固的精神沙漏
the most stubborn psychological filter that we have,

338
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:53,310
而当我们真正抵达其下面后
and that when we start really reaching down below that,

339
00:17:53,420 --> 00:17:55,210
当我们开始真正搞明白
when we start really figuring out

340
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,350
时间是如何由大脑构建的后
how time is constructed by the brain,

341
00:17:57,460 --> 00:17:59,650
我们将不得不回到物理学里
we're going to have to go back to physics

342
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:02,550
重整所有的计算公式
and rejig all of the equations there.

343
00:18:02,670 --> 00:18:06,420
弗里曼：是否有可能排出人为因素
Is it possible to eliminate the human factor

344
00:18:06,540 --> 00:18:08,090
把时间整个
and pull time completely out

345
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:10,590
从我们对宇宙的物理描述中拉出来呢？
of our physical description of the Universe?

346
00:18:10,710 --> 00:18:13,700
此人说 “可以”
This man says "yes."

347
00:18:13,810 --> 00:18:16,100
他重整了爱因斯坦的方程式
He's rejigged Einstein's equations,

348
00:18:16,210 --> 00:18:20,610
他发现时间可能根本就不存在
and he's found that time may not exist at all.

349
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:27,070
断言时间是个假象
Declaring that time is an illusion

350
00:18:27,190 --> 00:18:28,410
可能听上去很激进
may sound radical,

351
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:31,850
不过拒绝时间是个古老的想法——
but the denial of time is an old idea --

352
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:35,720
2500年之久了
2,500 years old.

353
00:18:35,830 --> 00:18:40,290
公元前500年 哲学家巴门尼德
In 500 B.C.,the philosopher Parmenides

354
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:43,190
宣称运动是不可能的
declared that motion is impossible

355
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:45,690
因为对于一个物体要移动一段距离
because for an object to move any distance,

356
00:18:45,810 --> 00:18:47,330
必须经过
it would have to pass through

357
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:49,760
无穷极数的分步
an infinite series of fractional steps

358
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:52,170
才能够从一处到另一处
to get from one place to another,

359
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:55,900
没有人能采取无穷的步骤
and no one can take infinite steps.

360
00:18:56,020 --> 00:19:00,570
如果运动是不可能的 那么变化也是不可能的
And if motion is impossible,then change is also impossible.

361
00:19:00,690 --> 00:19:03,980
因而 时间必定是个假象
So,therefore,time must be an illusion.

362
00:19:04,090 --> 00:19:07,380
没人明了此中缘故
No one knew quite what to make of this.

363
00:19:07,490 --> 00:19:09,450
当然 运动是真实的
Surely,motion is real.

364
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:13,730
事物确实改变了 时间确实流逝了 对吧？
Things do change and time does pass,right?

365
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:19,160
难说
Maybe not.

366
00:19:19,270 --> 00:19:22,130
在英国一个古老的乡村里
In an ancient village in the English countryside,

367
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:25,230
此人认为量子物理定律证明了
this man thinks that the laws of quantum physics prove

368
00:19:25,350 --> 00:19:28,100
巴门尼德是正确的
that Parmenides was right.

369
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:33,140
此人名叫朱利安.巴伯
His name is Julian Barbour.

370
00:19:33,250 --> 00:19:36,740
几十年前 他就着手精心安排一个数学案例
Decades ago,he began carefully laying out a mathematical case

371
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:40,550
阐述宇宙并不需要时间
that the universe doesn't need time,

372
00:19:40,660 --> 00:19:47,320
这有点怪怪的 因为他周遭都是过去
which is a bit odd,as he's surrounded by the past.

373
00:19:47,430 --> 00:19:52,330
我们站在小镇上 这是一条古街
We're standing in the town,which is a very ancient street,

374
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:56,500
我的身后是我的家 建于1659年
and behind me is my home,built 1659.

375
00:19:56,610 --> 00:19:58,300
当年牛顿17岁
Newton was 17 then,

376
00:19:58,410 --> 00:20:01,470
才开始认真考虑时间和运动
just seriously beginning to think about time and motion.

377
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:05,060
弗里曼：若时间并不存在
If time doesn't exist,

378
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:08,730
那这一切都是什么呢？
what's all this?

379
00:20:08,850 --> 00:20:13,640
对朱利安来说 我们所见的一切都是考古挖掘
To Julian,everything we see is an archaeological dig.

380
00:20:13,750 --> 00:20:16,040
物体问世在先
Things are there first,

381
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:19,910
时间是其后来的推断
and time is deduced from it afterwards.

382
00:20:20,030 --> 00:20:23,380
他认为这座千年教堂
He believes this 1,000-year-old church

383
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,890
这些14世纪的壁画
and these 14th-century wall paintings

384
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:30,960
就是整个时间存在于空间片段里的明证
are proof that the whole of time exists in slices of space.

385
00:20:31,070 --> 00:20:34,930
巴伯：我们的过去只是另一个世界
Our past is just another world,

386
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:38,470
或是宇宙另一个可能的布局
or it's another possible configuration of the Universe.

387
00:20:38,580 --> 00:20:40,180
它现在是另一个了
It's another now.

388
00:20:44,290 --> 00:20:46,410
这是真真切切的
And this is literally true.

389
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:50,060
片刻并不属于时间 时间就在片刻之中
The instant is not in time. Time is in the instant.

390
00:20:52,390 --> 00:20:54,680
弗里曼：朱利安激进的时间观
Julian's radical view of time

391
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:57,650
出自惠勒 - 德威特方程式
grows out of the Wheeler-DeWitt equation,

392
00:20:57,770 --> 00:21:01,090
一个20世纪60年代的数学习题
a mathematical exercise from the 1960s

393
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:04,630
它试图协调爱因斯坦的相对论
that sought to reconcile Einstein's relativity

394
00:21:04,740 --> 00:21:07,100
与量子力学这两者
with quantum mechanics.

395
00:21:07,210 --> 00:21:10,100
怪事就发生在你做此事时
A strange thing happens when you do this.

396
00:21:10,210 --> 00:21:14,800
你在方程式左边没有表示时间的"T"
You're left with an equation that has no "T" for time.

397
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:19,680
因为运算与观察到的现实背道而驰
Since this runs counter to observable reality,

398
00:21:19,790 --> 00:21:22,610
多数人认为方程式进一步证明了
most saw the equation as further proof

399
00:21:22,730 --> 00:21:25,580
量子物理与相对论
that quantum physics and relativity theory

400
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:27,230
无法和谐相处
don't play well together.

401
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:32,460
然而对朱利安来说 这是个启示
But to Julian,it was a revelation.

402
00:21:32,570 --> 00:21:36,630
量子力学并无独特的历史
There is no unique history in quantum mechanics.

403
00:21:36,740 --> 00:21:37,800
若是有证据
And if the evidence

404
00:21:37,910 --> 00:21:40,430
出自将量子力学与
from the attempts to combine quantum mechanics

405
00:21:40,550 --> 00:21:43,000
爱因斯坦的广义相对论合并起来的尝试是正确的话,
with Einstein's general relativity is right,

406
00:21:43,110 --> 00:21:44,340
那就根本没有时间
there is no time at all.

407
00:21:44,450 --> 00:21:47,640
弗里曼：因此在最深层次的现实中
So at the deepest level of reality,

408
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:49,740
时间并不存在
time doesn't exist.

409
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:53,050
问题是物体是如何相互协调相处在
What matters is how objects relate to each other

410
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:56,210
空间的凝固画面中的呢
in freeze frames of space.

411
00:21:56,330 --> 00:21:57,850
我眼中的宇宙 -
My view of the Universe --

412
00:21:57,960 --> 00:22:00,720
就像是一大堆快照
it's just like a huge collection of snapshots

413
00:22:00,830 --> 00:22:04,420
经过了极其丰富的编排
which are immensely,richly structured.

414
00:22:04,540 --> 00:22:07,960
它们彼此没有任何沟通
They're not in any communication with each other.

415
00:22:08,070 --> 00:22:10,130
它们的世界各自为政
They're worlds unto themselves.

416
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:12,800
然而每个世界都丰富多彩
But each world is so rich

417
00:22:12,910 --> 00:22:15,940
就是 可以这么说 是这个世界的一部分
that it's,so to speak,part of this world.

418
00:22:16,050 --> 00:22:17,940
快照里有快照
It's snapshots within snapshots.

419
00:22:18,050 --> 00:22:21,470
这其实就是我们生命的意义
This is really what our life is about.

420
00:22:21,590 --> 00:22:23,980
弗里曼：我们的大脑收集这些凝固的时刻
Our brains assemble these frozen moments

421
00:22:24,090 --> 00:22:25,310
在我们的脑海里播放
and play them in our minds

422
00:22:25,420 --> 00:22:27,980
同样那些静态的照片
the same way that still photographs

423
00:22:28,090 --> 00:22:30,080
每秒24帧播放
played at 24 frames per second

424
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:34,220
使得你现在所看到的图像似乎动了起来
make the images you're watching now seem to move.

425
00:22:34,330 --> 00:22:37,260
然而什么都没动
But nothing is moving.

426
00:22:37,370 --> 00:22:41,340
我们所谓的时间是一种假象
What we call "time" is an illusion.

427
00:22:43,880 --> 00:22:46,370
巴伯：在某些深刻的意义上
In some very deep sense,

428
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:49,300
宇宙 量子宇宙
the Universe,the quantum universe,

429
00:22:49,410 --> 00:22:50,870
只不过是静态的
is just static.

430
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:52,300
没有变化
Nothing changes.

431
00:22:52,420 --> 00:22:54,240
弗里曼：按朱利安的说法
And according to Julian,

432
00:22:54,350 --> 00:22:56,380
所有这些宇宙快照
all of these snapshots of the Universe

433
00:22:56,490 --> 00:23:00,210
是同时存在的
exist simultaneously.

434
00:23:00,330 --> 00:23:05,750
如果我说我的昨天已不复存在
If I were to say that my yesterday no longer exists,

435
00:23:05,860 --> 00:23:10,160
那就像是13号说11号已经死了
it would be like the number 13 saying that 11 has died.

436
00:23:10,270 --> 00:23:13,560
数学家视其为荒谬
Mathematicians would regard that as ridiculous.

437
00:23:13,670 --> 00:23:16,760
这个片刻非常重要 非常生动
This instant is so vital and so alive,

438
00:23:16,880 --> 00:23:19,330
但某种程度 它又是永恒的
but in a way,it's eternal.

439
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:22,300
此时你将它翻译成数学
This when you translate that into mathematics,

440
00:23:22,410 --> 00:23:24,080
它就是永恒的
it's eternal.

441
00:23:27,220 --> 00:23:31,340
朱利安.巴伯的时间观可能听上去很激进
Julian Barbour's view of time may sound radical,

442
00:23:31,460 --> 00:23:35,050
然而它得到了物理学界的认真对待
but it's taken very seriously by the physics community,

443
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:37,950
这并不意味着大家都同意他的说法
which doesn't mean everyone agrees with him.

444
00:23:38,060 --> 00:23:39,290
远非如此
Far from it.

445
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:41,590
朱利安的挚友李.施莫林
Julian's close friend Lee Smolin

446
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:43,590
还是他的最大的批评家之一
is also one of his biggest critics.

447
00:23:43,700 --> 00:23:45,930
施莫林：时间不是假象
Time is not an illusion.

448
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:48,930
时间不是构建
Time is not a construction.

449
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:51,330
时间不是突现
Time is not emergent.

450
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:54,530
时间是实实在在的
Time really is real.

451
00:23:54,650 --> 00:23:56,900
时间是假象的概念
The idea that time is an illusion

452
00:23:57,020 --> 00:23:59,470
引发了物理学上的内战 -
has ignited a civil war in physics --

453
00:23:59,580 --> 00:24:03,350
同室操戈
a war that pits friend against friend.

454
00:24:08,580 --> 00:24:14,580
时间是我们创造的用来理解宇宙的假象么？
Is time an illusion we create to make sense of the Universe?

455
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:18,610
神经学家和物理学家称它有可能是这样的
Neurologists and physicists say it might be so.

456
00:24:18,720 --> 00:24:21,170
但还有一个阵营称我们不能忽视
But there's another camp that says we can't ignore

457
00:24:21,280 --> 00:24:24,040
我们的感知和观察所告诉我们的
what our senses and observations tell us,

458
00:24:24,150 --> 00:24:28,350
时间确实存在
that time really does exist.

459
00:24:31,290 --> 00:24:33,120
按这种观点
In this view,

460
00:24:33,230 --> 00:24:36,190
我们感受的世界是时光流逝
we experience the world as a flow of moments

461
00:24:36,300 --> 00:24:38,720
因为那就是大自然的运作
because that's the way nature is.

462
00:24:38,830 --> 00:24:42,490
时光流逝是基本的道理
Passage of time is a basic truth

463
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:48,430
事实上 或许是宇宙中的一大实情
and,in fact,may be the one true thing in the Universe.

464
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:51,670
蒂姆.莫大林是罗格斯大学物理学哲学家
Tim Maudlin is a philosopher of physics

465
00:24:51,780 --> 00:24:53,450
蒂姆.莫大林是罗格斯大学物理学哲学家
at Rutgers University.

466
00:24:55,220 --> 00:24:57,910
要说时光流逝真是个假象
To say that the passage of time is really an illusion

467
00:24:58,020 --> 00:25:00,780
表明那并非真的是那个样子
suggests that it's not really,really the case

468
00:25:00,890 --> 00:25:02,780
我一直都在变老
that I'm getting older all the time,

469
00:25:02,890 --> 00:25:06,520
我该担心我的辞世 每天
that I should be worried that my death is,every day,

470
00:25:06,630 --> 00:25:09,090
有朝一日死到临头 等等
one day closer to me and so on.

471
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:12,060
不过我简直就不能相信
But I just can't believe that.

472
00:25:12,170 --> 00:25:15,090
我试着去努力 但我不能相信
As hard as I try,I can't believe it,

473
00:25:15,210 --> 00:25:17,300
它并不适合我所生活的世界
and it doesn't fit with the world I live in.

474
00:25:17,410 --> 00:25:19,160
弗里曼：对蒂姆来说
For Tim,

475
00:25:19,280 --> 00:25:23,570
这只是时间存在的常识
it is just common sense that time exists.

476
00:25:23,680 --> 00:25:27,410
那为什么有些物理学家否认它呢？
So,why do some physicists deny it?

477
00:25:27,520 --> 00:25:30,280
蒂姆认为这是职业病
Tim thinks it's an occupational hazard

478
00:25:30,390 --> 00:25:32,580
与数学打交道就是这样
of working with math.

479
00:25:32,690 --> 00:25:35,550
我们物理学中的表述都是数学
Our representations in physics are all mathematical,

480
00:25:35,660 --> 00:25:37,520
数学对象并不在乎时间
and mathematical objects are not in time.

481
00:25:37,630 --> 00:25:39,920
数学对象并不变化
Mathematical objects don't change.

482
00:25:40,030 --> 00:25:43,830
所以 若是你与数字打太多的交道
So,if you work too much with numbers

483
00:25:43,940 --> 00:25:46,290
数字是不会变化的
and numbers don't change

484
00:25:46,410 --> 00:25:48,760
你用它来代表世界
and you're using that to represent the world,

485
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,130
似乎就很难看到
it might seem hard to see

486
00:25:50,240 --> 00:25:53,100
世界本身在如何变化
how the world itself can really be changing.

487
00:25:53,210 --> 00:25:55,500
人们似乎被这种概念难住了
People seem to be stuck on the idea

488
00:25:55,620 --> 00:25:57,470
即世界具有数学特性
that the world has the features

489
00:25:57,580 --> 00:25:59,810
这被用来表述它
of the mathematics that they use to represent it.

490
00:25:59,920 --> 00:26:01,070
那就让人们
That allowed people

491
00:26:01,190 --> 00:26:03,740
痴迷于他们的数学
to get carried away with their mathematics

492
00:26:03,860 --> 00:26:06,250
而无视物理世界
and lose sight of the physical world.

493
00:26:06,360 --> 00:26:08,280
弗里曼：朱利安.巴伯认为
Julian Barbour believes

494
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:12,790
空间是明摆着的 而时间则是假象
space is all there is and time is an illusion.

495
00:26:12,900 --> 00:26:16,420
蒂姆说朱利安全都错了
Tim says Julian has got it all wrong.

496
00:26:16,540 --> 00:26:20,800
我们需要时间 但我们不需要空间
We need time,but we don't need space.

497
00:26:20,910 --> 00:26:23,600
莫大林：我们可以让空间无关紧要
We can make space not fundamental,

498
00:26:23,710 --> 00:26:25,870
但时间要保持根本性
but time remains fundamental.

499
00:26:25,980 --> 00:26:28,300
必定不存在什么能比得过时间的
There doesn't have to be anything more than time,

500
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:30,140
反之是行不通的
and you can't do it the other way around.

501
00:26:30,250 --> 00:26:32,210
你得先有空间 然后才有时间
You have to start with space and then get time.

502
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:36,510
所以时间是最基本的东西
So,time is at the very bottom level.

503
00:26:36,620 --> 00:26:38,910
我甚至觉得这就是物理学所告诉我们的
I think even this is what the physics is telling us,

504
00:26:39,030 --> 00:26:41,530
尽管我们对其没有表现出足够的关注
although we haven't been paying enough attention to it.

505
00:26:43,360 --> 00:26:45,590
弗里曼：是空间先出现呢…
Did space come first...

506
00:26:45,700 --> 00:26:47,890
还是时间先出现呢？
Or did time come first?

507
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:50,130
这个争论一直倒回到
This argument leads all the way back

508
00:26:50,240 --> 00:26:52,630
我们宇宙的突然诞生——
to the explosive birth of our Universe --

509
00:26:52,740 --> 00:26:54,170
大爆炸
the Big Bang.

510
00:26:57,110 --> 00:27:01,270
物理学家同意大爆炸开辟了空间
Physicists agree that the Big Bang created space.

511
00:27:01,380 --> 00:27:06,120
他们不同意它是否也创造了时间
They don't agree on whether it also created time.

512
00:27:10,530 --> 00:27:13,380
斯莫林：物理学和哲学里有许多人
There's a lot of people in physics and philosophy

513
00:27:13,500 --> 00:27:15,480
认为时间是假象
who think that time is an illusion,

514
00:27:15,600 --> 00:27:16,820
真理是什么
that what's really true

515
00:27:16,930 --> 00:27:19,690
在最深层面上的永恒的
at the deepest,deepest level is timeless,

516
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:21,860
是超越时间
is outside of time.

517
00:27:21,970 --> 00:27:23,220
我可不那么认为
And I don't believe that.

518
00:27:23,340 --> 00:27:24,830
我曾经那么认为过
I used to believe that,

519
00:27:24,940 --> 00:27:26,390
但我后来认为
but I've come to believe

520
00:27:26,510 --> 00:27:28,660
时间是千真万确的现实
that time is really,really real.

521
00:27:28,780 --> 00:27:30,200
弗里曼：李.斯莫林认为
Lee Smolin believes

522
00:27:30,310 --> 00:27:33,370
时间比宇宙还年长——
that time is older than the Universe --

523
00:27:33,480 --> 00:27:36,170
它在大爆炸之前就存在了
it was here before the Big Bang,

524
00:27:36,280 --> 00:27:38,570
它在宇宙终结后还将存在
and it will be here after the Universe ends.

525
00:27:38,690 --> 00:27:41,840
他认为他能够证明这它
And he thinks he can prove it

526
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:45,480
通过仔细观察光子的
by looking closely at how particles of light behave

527
00:27:45,590 --> 00:27:47,580
长距离行为
over long distances.

528
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:50,220
物理学的核心规律之一规定
One of the core laws of physics states

529
00:27:50,330 --> 00:27:55,290
光速是每秒186,282英里
that light travels at 186,282 miles per second.

530
00:27:55,400 --> 00:27:57,860
如果时间是假象
If time is an illusion,

531
00:27:57,970 --> 00:28:02,100
那真的就会是在宇宙各个角落
then this will be true everywhere in the Universe,

532
00:28:02,210 --> 00:28:04,500
并没有我们所看到的物质存在了
no matter where we look.

533
00:28:04,610 --> 00:28:07,240
但如果时间是真实存在的
But if time is real,

534
00:28:07,350 --> 00:28:10,940
那就有可能物理定律会随着
it's possible that the laws of physics have changed

535
00:28:11,050 --> 00:28:14,680
宇宙的年长而改变
as the Universe has aged.

536
00:28:14,790 --> 00:28:17,980
若是如光速这样的基本物理定律
If a basic law of physics such as the speed of light

537
00:28:18,090 --> 00:28:21,580
并不适用于宇宙的最古老部分的话
doesn't hold true out in the oldest part of the Universe,

538
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:24,350
那么我们将会知道物理学自宇宙诞生以来
we'll know that physics has evolved

539
00:28:24,470 --> 00:28:26,860
已经演变了
since the Universe was born,

540
00:28:26,970 --> 00:28:31,390
因而时间不能是假象
so time can't be an illusion.

541
00:28:31,510 --> 00:28:32,960
会有某些实验的
There should be some experiments

542
00:28:33,080 --> 00:28:34,900
这样 如果你很敏感地观察的话
where,if you look very sensitively,

543
00:28:35,010 --> 00:28:37,700
或许光速并不具有普遍性
maybe the speed of light is not Universal.

544
00:28:37,810 --> 00:28:40,520
这样的实验有正在进行的
And there are such experiments which are being done.

545
00:28:42,420 --> 00:28:44,210
弗里曼：费米太空望远镜
The Fermi Space Telescope

546
00:28:44,320 --> 00:28:46,240
就是这样一个实验
is one such experiment.

547
00:28:46,360 --> 00:28:49,310
费米将记录伽马射线暴——
Fermi records gamma-ray bursts --

548
00:28:49,430 --> 00:28:51,820
怪异的能量暴发
strange blasts of energy

549
00:28:51,930 --> 00:28:54,420
来自宇宙的最远端
from the farthest reaches of the Universe.

550
00:28:54,530 --> 00:28:58,350
这些爆发给我们机会去检查物理规律
These bursts give us the chance to check out the laws of physics

551
00:28:58,470 --> 00:29:01,740
在130亿年前的模样
as they were 13 billion years ago.

552
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:06,460
试想有两个光子从100亿光年远的
Imagine two photons race out of a gamma-ray burst

553
00:29:06,580 --> 00:29:09,500
伽马射线暴竞相闯出来
10 billion light-years away.

554
00:29:09,610 --> 00:29:14,950
其中一个光子获得的能量大于另一个
One photon bursts with more energy than the other.

555
00:29:16,520 --> 00:29:18,880
在我们这部分宇宙里
In our part of the Universe,

556
00:29:18,990 --> 00:29:23,780
两个光子会以完全相同的速度穿行
both photons will travel at exactly the same speed.

557
00:29:23,890 --> 00:29:25,850
但若是光的物理性质
But if the physics of light are different

558
00:29:25,960 --> 00:29:28,490
在较老部分的宇宙间有所不同
in an older part of the Universe,

559
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:31,320
李认为较高能量的光子
Lee believes the higher-energy photon

560
00:29:31,430 --> 00:29:33,570
应该稍稍落后
should fall slightly behind.

561
00:29:37,470 --> 00:29:39,330
斯莫林：平衡的打破将会在那里
It would break down at the point where,

562
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:41,270
100亿年之后
after 10 billion years,

563
00:29:41,380 --> 00:29:43,370
其中之一将会一秒 或二秒 或三秒领先
one of them would be a second or two or three seconds ahead,

564
00:29:43,480 --> 00:29:47,470
但那足以被检测到
but that's enough to be detected.

565
00:29:47,590 --> 00:29:50,340
即使是100亿年之一秒——
Even one second worth over 10 billion years --

566
00:29:50,460 --> 00:29:51,710
我们也能检测到
we can detect that.

567
00:29:51,820 --> 00:29:54,180
弗里曼：费米发出的伽马射线暴的数据
The gamma-ray burst data from Fermi

568
00:29:54,290 --> 00:29:56,880
会在接下来几年里送达
will come in over the next few years.

569
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,150
李可能很快就有他的证据了
Lee may soon have his proof

570
00:29:59,270 --> 00:30:02,320
那就是130亿年前的现在
that the now of 13 billion years ago

571
00:30:02,440 --> 00:30:05,160
这是不同于我们的现在
is truly different from our now,

572
00:30:05,270 --> 00:30:09,000
因而 时间必定是真实的
and therefore,time must be real.

573
00:30:09,110 --> 00:30:13,100
物理定律随着时间而改变的确凿证据
Conclusive proof that the laws of physics change over time

574
00:30:13,210 --> 00:30:14,800
将会解决这个争论——
would settle the debate

575
00:30:14,910 --> 00:30:18,570
时间究竟是真实还是假象
over whether time is real or an illusion.

576
00:30:18,680 --> 00:30:22,740
但还是留下了一个大问题未予解决——
But it still leaves a big question unanswered --

577
00:30:22,850 --> 00:30:25,280
为什么会有时间呢？
why is there time?

578
00:30:25,390 --> 00:30:28,920
理论上 物理学似乎并不需要时间
In theory,physics doesn't seem to need time,

579
00:30:29,030 --> 00:30:32,490
然而我们自我感觉穿行其中
and yet we feel ourselves moving through it.

580
00:30:32,600 --> 00:30:35,490
如果时间不是我们头脑里天生的
If time wasn't born in our minds,

581
00:30:35,600 --> 00:30:37,800
那么它又是从哪里来的呢？
then where did it come from?

582
00:30:39,540 --> 00:30:42,100
肖恩.卡罗尔认为他有了答案
Sean Carroll thinks he has the answer.

583
00:30:42,210 --> 00:30:45,770
但是它需要邪恶孪生宇宙
But it takes an evil-twin Universe

584
00:30:45,880 --> 00:30:49,710
与后退的时间一道才能使其奏效
with backward-flowing time to make it all work.

585
00:30:54,380 --> 00:30:57,300
关于时间如何运作的理论大量充斥于
Theories abound about how time works,

586
00:30:57,420 --> 00:31:00,640
宇宙间和我们的头脑里
in the Universe and in our minds.

587
00:31:01,550 --> 00:31:05,180
但就是有一位难得一见的物理学家 提出了问题
But it's a rare physicist who asks the question,

588
00:31:05,290 --> 00:31:07,980
为什么会有时间呢？
"Why is there time?"

589
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:11,420
如果时间不是我们人类发明的东西
If time isn't something we humans invented,

590
00:31:11,530 --> 00:31:15,190
那它又是从何而来的呢？
then where did it come from?

591
00:31:15,300 --> 00:31:19,860
肖恩.卡罗尔认为他知道
Sean Carroll thinks he knows.

592
00:31:19,980 --> 00:31:22,530
肖恩是一位理论物理学家
Sean is a theoretical physicist

593
00:31:22,650 --> 00:31:25,640
供职于加州理工学院
at the California Institute of Technology.

594
00:31:25,750 --> 00:31:26,940
时间是实实在在的东西
Time is real.

595
00:31:27,050 --> 00:31:29,570
我们每天都在用它 证据在我们身边比比皆是
We use it every day. The evidence is all around us.

596
00:31:29,690 --> 00:31:30,840
然而作为科学家
But as scientists,

597
00:31:30,950 --> 00:31:33,110
我们对时间的真正意义思考得越多
the more we think about what time really means,

598
00:31:33,220 --> 00:31:34,780
它就越扑朔迷离
the more mysterious it becomes.

599
00:31:34,890 --> 00:31:37,480
弗里曼：肖恩接受常识性的想法
Sean accepts the common-sense idea

600
00:31:37,590 --> 00:31:41,150
即时间是往前移动的 从过去到未来
that time moves forward from the past to the future,

601
00:31:41,260 --> 00:31:42,820
就像箭头一般
like an arrow.

602
00:31:42,930 --> 00:31:45,790
但为何时间会有方向？
But why does time have a direction?

603
00:31:45,900 --> 00:31:48,490
肖恩认为答案
Sean believes the answer is closely tied

604
00:31:48,600 --> 00:31:51,840
与焦作熵的东西息息相关
to something called entropy.

605
00:31:57,380 --> 00:32:00,540
让时间成为特别的是物理学定律
What makes time special is a law of physics,

606
00:32:00,650 --> 00:32:01,970
热力学第二定律
the second law of thermodynamics.

607
00:32:02,080 --> 00:32:03,810
第二定律基本上说
The second law essentially says

608
00:32:03,920 --> 00:32:06,310
随着时间的推移 熵在增大
that as time goes on,entropy increases.

609
00:32:06,420 --> 00:32:10,250
熵告诉我们情况有多凌乱
Entropy is telling us how messy things are,

610
00:32:10,360 --> 00:32:13,150
宇宙中的情况有多无序 有多混乱
how disorderly,how chaotic things are in the Universe.

611
00:32:13,260 --> 00:32:14,420
而在过去
So in the past,

612
00:32:14,530 --> 00:32:16,420
若是你一路回到早期的宇宙
if you go all the way back to the early Universe,

613
00:32:16,530 --> 00:32:17,950
那是非常有序的
it was very organized.

614
00:32:18,070 --> 00:32:20,520
那就像是这些精巧排列的
It was like this delicately arranged configuration

615
00:32:20,640 --> 00:32:21,860
台球
of billiard balls.

616
00:32:21,970 --> 00:32:24,190
随着时间的推移 就像是我们在打台球一样 -
As time goes on,it's like we're playing pool --

617
00:32:24,310 --> 00:32:25,870
首先我们要做的…
the first thing we do...

618
00:32:27,610 --> 00:32:31,170
…是我们要增加宇宙的混乱
...Is we increase the chaos of the Universe.

619
00:32:31,280 --> 00:32:33,600
宇宙间时间的推移是个整体
As time goes on in the Universe as a whole,

620
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:36,520
无序 熵升高了
disorderliness,entropy goes up.

621
00:32:38,720 --> 00:32:41,680
弗里曼：因为宇宙的突然面世
Since the explosive birth of the Universe,

622
00:32:41,790 --> 00:32:44,010
熵的增大就决定了
the increase of entropy is the reason

623
00:32:44,130 --> 00:32:47,550
为什么过去不同于未来…
why the past is different from the future...

624
00:32:47,660 --> 00:32:51,290
为什么会有时间箭头…
Why there is an arrow of time...

625
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:53,650
为什么我们记得过去…
Why we remember the past...

626
00:32:53,770 --> 00:32:55,890
为什么我们会变老…
Why we grow older...

627
00:32:56,000 --> 00:32:59,060
为什么进化会是这种方式
Why evolution happens the way it does.

628
00:32:59,170 --> 00:33:04,440
这一切都是源于这个熵的增大
It's all because of this increase of entropy.

629
00:33:06,110 --> 00:33:09,110
那奥秘何在呢？ 熵随着时间而提高
So,where's the mystery? Entropy goes up as time goes on.

630
00:33:09,230 --> 00:33:10,230
但有趣的是
But interestingly,

631
00:33:10,340 --> 00:33:12,210
在支撑我们周围一切的
in the fundamental laws of physics

632
00:33:12,320 --> 00:33:13,940
基本物理定律中
underlying everything around us,

633
00:33:14,060 --> 00:33:16,510
过去与未来之间并无差异
there is no difference between the past and the future.

634
00:33:16,630 --> 00:33:19,820
流传给我们的定律 不管是牛顿
The laws handed down to us by Isaac Newton,

635
00:33:19,930 --> 00:33:22,290
爱因斯坦 乃至量子力学
Albert Einstein,even in quantum mechanics,

636
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:23,620
你都无法区分
you have no distinction

637
00:33:23,730 --> 00:33:26,760
一个方向的时间与另一个方向的时间的差异
between one direction of time and the other.

638
00:33:26,870 --> 00:33:29,130
所以 如果你有一个非常简单的物理系统
So,if you have a very simple physical system,

639
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:30,590
比如就两个台球
like just two billiard balls,

640
00:33:30,710 --> 00:33:31,970
当你将一个撞上另一个…
when you knock one into the other...

641
00:33:34,340 --> 00:33:35,670
…一个方向的时间
...There is no difference

642
00:33:35,780 --> 00:33:37,200
与另一个并无差别
between one direction of time and the other.

643
00:33:37,310 --> 00:33:38,970
你可以回放影像
You could play that movie backwards,

644
00:33:39,080 --> 00:33:40,370
它会看上去很正常
it would look perfectly normal.

645
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:43,310
只有当我们碰到复杂的宏观系统时
It's only when we get to complicated,macroscopic systems

646
00:33:43,420 --> 00:33:46,310
过去与未来之间就有差异了
that there's a difference between the past and the future.

647
00:33:46,420 --> 00:33:48,580
当我们把许多台球放在台球桌上时
When we have lots of balls on the billiard table,

648
00:33:48,690 --> 00:33:50,410
情况就发生在时间的一个方向上
things happen in one direction of time

649
00:33:50,530 --> 00:33:51,610
而不是其它方向
but not the other.

650
00:33:51,730 --> 00:33:54,060
或者还是当台球厅里形势失控之时呢
Or when all hell breaks loose in the pool hall.

651
00:34:03,510 --> 00:34:06,300
好 现在我们热闹了
So,now we have noise,

652
00:34:06,410 --> 00:34:09,070
玻璃破碎 血肉横飞
breaking glass,blood splattering.

653
00:34:09,180 --> 00:34:10,200
这就是宇宙熵
These are all processes

654
00:34:10,310 --> 00:34:12,300
增大的整个过程
that increase the entropy of the Universe.

655
00:34:12,420 --> 00:34:15,110
加在一起 所有这些熵的增大
Together,all of these increases of entropy

656
00:34:15,220 --> 00:34:16,640
就界定了时间之箭
define the arrow of time.

657
00:34:16,750 --> 00:34:17,940
问题是
The question is,

658
00:34:18,050 --> 00:34:21,010
为何熵在一开始时会如此之低呢？
why was the entropy so low to begin with?

659
00:34:21,120 --> 00:34:23,710
我们的宇宙失去了平衡
Our Universe seems to be out of balance.

660
00:34:23,830 --> 00:34:25,010
遥远的未来
The far,far future

661
00:34:25,130 --> 00:34:27,920
将会是个非常非常混乱的地方
is going to be a very,very disorganized place,

662
00:34:28,030 --> 00:34:31,090
但是遥远的过去却是高度有序的
but the far,far past was highly organized.

663
00:34:31,200 --> 00:34:34,470
作为物理学家 这种不稳定确实令我们烦恼
As physicists,this kind of imbalance really bugs us.

664
00:34:39,240 --> 00:34:41,300
弗里曼：肖恩在寻求能解释
Sean looked for an explanation

665
00:34:41,410 --> 00:34:43,670
这种时间的不稳定
of this imbalance of time,

666
00:34:43,780 --> 00:34:46,340
他发现它就在多元宇宙中
and he found it in the multiverse.

667
00:34:46,450 --> 00:34:49,740
根据这个理论 我们所看到的宇宙
According to this theory,the Universe we see

668
00:34:49,850 --> 00:34:54,680
可以是无限个宇宙中的一个
could be one of an infinite number of Universes.

669
00:34:54,790 --> 00:34:57,050
卡罗尔：设想有一个妈咪宇宙
Imagine a mommy Universe.

670
00:34:57,160 --> 00:34:58,620
那么这个妈咪宇宙
So,this mommy Universe

671
00:34:58,730 --> 00:35:01,260
基本上可以生出宇宙宝贝来
can essentially give birth to baby Universes.

672
00:35:03,100 --> 00:35:04,990
一个小小的量子波动
A little quantum fluctuation

673
00:35:05,100 --> 00:35:08,830
可以产生一个空间泡沫 开始很小 然后长大 -
can make a bubble of space that starts small and then grows --

674
00:35:08,940 --> 00:35:12,330
开始是熵很低 然后熵不断增大
starts with low entropy and then increases in entropy,

675
00:35:12,440 --> 00:35:14,130
就像我们的宇宙这般
just like our Universe does.

676
00:35:14,240 --> 00:35:16,500
弗里曼：这样 妈咪宇宙
So,a mother Universe

677
00:35:16,610 --> 00:35:19,440
就生出了一个我们这样的宇宙——
gives birth to a Universe like ours --

678
00:35:19,550 --> 00:35:24,170
一个时间箭头一直往前的宇宙
a Universe where the arrow of time moves forward.

679
00:35:24,290 --> 00:35:26,040
但要保持平衡
But to stay in balance,

680
00:35:26,160 --> 00:35:29,350
它还得生出一个镜像宇宙
it also has to give birth to a mirror-image Universe,

681
00:35:29,460 --> 00:35:32,280
在其中时间是倒退的
where time moves backward.

682
00:35:32,390 --> 00:35:34,980
这意味着站在其它一些角度上
This means that in some other dimension,

683
00:35:35,100 --> 00:35:38,620
我们的宇宙有一个邪恶双胞胎
our Universe has an evil twin.

684
00:35:38,740 --> 00:35:41,760
每一个泡沫都是独自的宇宙 带有自己的时间箭头
Every bubble is its own Universe with its own arrow of time.

685
00:35:41,870 --> 00:35:44,400
在每个泡沫中 时间箭头似乎无暇可击
Within each bubble,the arrow of time seems fine,

686
00:35:44,510 --> 00:35:47,130
但若是你相互比较不同的泡沫
but if you compare different bubbles to each other,

687
00:35:47,240 --> 00:35:49,870
时间箭头将会是指向相反的方向
the arrows will be pointing in opposite directions.

688
00:35:49,980 --> 00:35:51,300
弗里曼：肖恩的多元宇宙理论
Sean's multiverse theory

689
00:35:51,420 --> 00:35:54,740
自推出以来就广受关注
has attracted a lot of attention since it was introduced.

690
00:35:54,850 --> 00:35:57,740
但那会被证明是时间之谜的
But will it prove to be the ultimate solution

691
00:35:57,860 --> 00:36:01,680
最终解决方案么？
to the mystery of time?

692
00:36:01,790 --> 00:36:04,280
这个 部分取得进展的物理学称
Well,part of making progress in physics is saying,

693
00:36:04,400 --> 00:36:06,620
说不定这是真的 说不定那是真的？
"What if this is true? What if that is true?"

694
00:36:06,730 --> 00:36:08,450
有时 在你说说不定的时候
And sometimes when you say "What if?"

695
00:36:08,570 --> 00:36:10,690
你会意识到 噢 做出那个假设的一跳
You realize,"Oh,making that hypothetical leap"

696
00:36:10,800 --> 00:36:13,120
确实有助于我们解决我们所有的这些问题
really helps us with all these problems we're having."

697
00:36:13,240 --> 00:36:15,030
而在其他时候 它只是给你个烂摊子
Other times,it just gets you in a mess.

698
00:36:15,140 --> 00:36:20,030
量子力学和多元宇宙理论
Quantum mechanics and the multiverse theory

699
00:36:20,140 --> 00:36:25,700
给了我们解决时间之谜困扰的有趣方法
give us interesting ways to grapple with the riddle of time.

700
00:36:25,820 --> 00:36:29,350
我们把弦论掺合进去后又会发生什么情况呢？
What happens when we add string theory into the mix?

701
00:36:30,650 --> 00:36:32,120
[变声] 天灵灵 地灵灵
Serious weirdness.

702
00:36:34,730 --> 00:36:37,890
时间之谜有许多潜在的解决方案——
The mystery of time has many possible solutions --

703
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:42,490
时间是绝对的 或是相对的
time is absolute or it is relative;

704
00:36:42,870 --> 00:36:44,890
时间是假象
time is an illusion

705
00:36:45,570 --> 00:36:49,060
或者它是熵的实实在在的产物
or it is the very real product of entropy.

706
00:36:49,550 --> 00:36:52,980
但是还有另外一个可能性——
But there is one other possibility --

707
00:36:53,090 --> 00:36:55,580
有个想法挑战了我们
an idea that challenges our assumptions

708
00:36:55,690 --> 00:37:00,180
关于昨日 今日 明日的假定
about yesterday,today,and tomorrow.

709
00:37:00,300 --> 00:37:04,450
对我们来说 时间的流动似乎是从左到右
To us,time seems to flow from left to right,

710
00:37:04,570 --> 00:37:08,960
但它若是还上下流动呢？
but what if it also goes up and down?

711
00:37:09,070 --> 00:37:13,360
若是时间像空间一样 有不止一个维度——
What if time,like space,has more than one dimension --

712
00:37:13,480 --> 00:37:18,340
有我们看不到的隐匿的维度呢？
a hidden dimension that we can't see?

713
00:37:18,450 --> 00:37:22,740
史蒂夫.温斯坦 周界物理研究所的一位科学家
Steve Weinstein,a scientist at the Perimeter Institute,

714
00:37:22,850 --> 00:37:25,180
认为这有可能是真的
thinks it could be true

715
00:37:25,290 --> 00:37:28,950
它有可能解决另外一大谜团——
and that it may solve another great mystery --

716
00:37:29,060 --> 00:37:31,150
量子不确定性之谜
the riddle of quantum uncertainty.

717
00:37:31,260 --> 00:37:34,930
史蒂夫是物理学家 哲学家
Steve is a physicist,philosopher,

718
00:37:35,040 --> 00:37:37,070
专业音乐家
and professional musician.

719
00:37:37,180 --> 00:37:39,140
他眼中的时间出自
His view of time grows out of

720
00:37:39,250 --> 00:37:43,140
数学最为集中的科学思想之一
one of the most mathematically dense ideas in science --

721
00:37:43,250 --> 00:37:44,770
弦论
string theory.

722
00:37:44,890 --> 00:37:47,310
弦论家认为
String theorists believe

723
00:37:47,420 --> 00:37:50,680
空间并不止我们所见到的三个维度
that space has more than the three dimensions we see.

724
00:37:50,790 --> 00:37:52,680
这就引得史蒂夫去思考
This got Steve to thinking

725
00:37:52,790 --> 00:37:56,550
同样的思想也可以用在时间上
that the same idea could be applied to time.

726
00:37:56,670 --> 00:37:58,020
温斯坦：我想 这个
I thought,"well,"

727
00:37:58,130 --> 00:38:01,220
为什么我们加给空间的维度如此慷慨
"Why do we multiply spatial dimensions so freely,

728
00:38:01,340 --> 00:38:02,560
而不给时间呢？
"but not time?

729
00:38:02,670 --> 00:38:04,260
告诉你 有什么好理由么？
"And,you know,is there any good reason?"

730
00:38:04,370 --> 00:38:06,130
所以这里存在一点好奇
So there was a sort of curiosity there.

731
00:38:06,240 --> 00:38:08,530
弗里曼：史蒂夫开始行动了
Steve set to work.

732
00:38:08,640 --> 00:38:11,300
时间一直被视为线状 -
Time has always been treated as a line --

733
00:38:11,410 --> 00:38:13,500
一维的东西
a one-dimensional thing.

734
00:38:13,610 --> 00:38:17,740
但如果时间具有两个维度 那时间就不是线状的了
But if time has two dimensions,then time isn't a line.

735
00:38:17,850 --> 00:38:19,040
它具有形状
It's a shape.

736
00:38:19,150 --> 00:38:21,540
温斯坦：你不妨看看这条长长的吉他电线
If you look at this guitar cable from far away,

737
00:38:21,660 --> 00:38:23,840
看上去就像是一维的物体
it looks like a one-dimensional object.

738
00:38:23,960 --> 00:38:25,310
它看上去就像是一条线
It just looks like a line.

739
00:38:25,430 --> 00:38:26,550
你若是凑近
If you get up close,

740
00:38:26,660 --> 00:38:29,880
你可以看到它有另一个维度
you can see that it has another dimension,

741
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:32,490
这必定涉及到电线的圆周
which has to do with the circumference of the cable.

742
00:38:32,600 --> 00:38:34,720
它就像是个圆柱体
It's like a cylinder.

743
00:38:34,830 --> 00:38:36,590
我们的世界看上去是三维的
Our world looks three-dimensional

744
00:38:36,700 --> 00:38:39,030
同样 这条长长的电线
in the same way that this cable from far away

745
00:38:39,140 --> 00:38:40,370
看起来是一维的
looks one-dimensional.

746
00:38:42,070 --> 00:38:45,830
弗里曼：根据史蒂夫的说法 如果时间有另外的维度
According to Steve,if time has an extra dimension,

747
00:38:45,950 --> 00:38:49,340
那么基本粒子如电子 质子
then fundamental particles like electrons and photons

748
00:38:49,450 --> 00:38:52,670
就会肆意穿越时间
are smeared across time.

749
00:38:52,790 --> 00:38:56,340
描述粒子的普通方式
So,an ordinary way of describing a particle

750
00:38:56,460 --> 00:38:58,380
就是讨论它在
would be to talk about its position

751
00:38:58,490 --> 00:38:59,710
任何时刻的位置
at any moment in time.

752
00:38:59,830 --> 00:39:01,950
粒子 或琴拨 可以在这里或这里
So the particle,or the pick,could be here

753
00:39:02,060 --> 00:39:04,520
这里 这里 这里
or here or here or here or here.

754
00:39:04,630 --> 00:39:06,650
所以 我如果要制作图表
So,if I were to graph that

755
00:39:06,770 --> 00:39:09,220
我把时间作为纵轴
and I had the time as a vertical axis,

756
00:39:09,340 --> 00:39:11,060
我就只能一直往上
I would just draw that.

757
00:39:11,170 --> 00:39:13,760
现在 如果你有另外的时间维度
Now,if you have an extra time dimension,

758
00:39:13,870 --> 00:39:16,600
你可以想象时间维度
you might visualize the time dimension

759
00:39:16,710 --> 00:39:19,370
垂直于琴颈
perpendicular to the guitar neck,

760
00:39:19,480 --> 00:39:20,900
在这个方向
in this direction.

761
00:39:21,010 --> 00:39:22,900
粒子就可以——
The particle could be --

762
00:39:23,020 --> 00:39:25,270
可以在这里
it might be here,

763
00:39:25,380 --> 00:39:28,570
可以在这里 可以到那里
and it might be here,and it might be over here.

764
00:39:28,690 --> 00:39:31,210
弗里曼：换句话说
To put it another way,

765
00:39:31,320 --> 00:39:34,650
量子理论告诉我们 亚原子粒子
quantum theory tells us that subatomic particles

766
00:39:34,760 --> 00:39:38,150
在空间居无定所
don't have definite addresses in space.

767
00:39:38,270 --> 00:39:41,390
我们只能猜测它们可能的住所
We can only guess where they probably live.

768
00:39:41,500 --> 00:39:45,290
史蒂夫怀疑它们得有住所
Steve suspects they do have addresses,

769
00:39:45,410 --> 00:39:47,530
但那些住所沿着
but those addresses are spread out

770
00:39:47,640 --> 00:39:49,730
时间额外的维度展开出去
across an extra dimension of time

771
00:39:49,850 --> 00:39:51,940
我们无法侦测到
that we can't detect.

772
00:39:53,150 --> 00:39:57,110
如是真的 这将颠覆物理学
If true,this revolutionizes physics.

773
00:39:57,220 --> 00:40:01,180
模糊的量子世界将突然一清二楚了
The fuzzy quantum world suddenly snaps into focus.

774
00:40:01,290 --> 00:40:02,510
遗憾的是
But unfortunately,

775
00:40:02,620 --> 00:40:05,080
证明二维时间是真实的
proving two-dimensional time is real

776
00:40:05,190 --> 00:40:08,820
或许是几乎不可能的
may be next to impossible.

777
00:40:08,930 --> 00:40:11,220
首先 它很难理解
For one thing,it's not easy to understand,

778
00:40:11,330 --> 00:40:13,390
甚至对其他物理学家
even for other physicists.

779
00:40:13,500 --> 00:40:16,290
描述宇宙所需的数学
The math required to describe a Universe

780
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:19,960
用于两个时间维度上实在难懂
with two dimensions of time is difficult.

781
00:40:20,070 --> 00:40:24,200
对于弦论的九个空间维度
Add in the nine spatial dimensions of string theory,

782
00:40:24,310 --> 00:40:27,150
人们的头脑爆炸了
and people's heads explode.

783
00:40:29,450 --> 00:40:32,240
这是个极具挑战的概念
It's very challenging conceptually.

784
00:40:32,350 --> 00:40:34,370
这是我所遇到的最艰难的问题
It's the hardest problem I've ever worked on,

785
00:40:34,490 --> 00:40:36,510
我想这就是为什么多数人都不去碰它的原因
and I think this is why more people don't do it.

786
00:40:36,620 --> 00:40:38,550
很难去思索这些术语——
It's very hard to think in these terms --

787
00:40:38,660 --> 00:40:40,660
额外的时间维度究竟意味着什么？
what would an extra time mean?

788
00:40:42,500 --> 00:40:43,620
弗里曼：然而
Nonetheless,

789
00:40:43,730 --> 00:40:47,350
史蒂夫认为值得一搏
Steve thinks it's worth the effort.

790
00:40:47,470 --> 00:40:49,390
温斯坦：多元时间是个途径
Multiple times is one way,

791
00:40:49,500 --> 00:40:52,990
或许是错误的途径 但它是个不同的途径——
possibly the wrong way,but it's a different way of --

792
00:40:53,100 --> 00:40:54,390
一个完全不同的途径——
and a radically different way --

793
00:40:54,510 --> 00:40:56,270
把物理世界概念化
of conceptualizing the physical world.

794
00:40:58,440 --> 00:41:00,670
弗里曼：物理学家探索时间之谜
The physicists exploring the mystery of time

795
00:41:00,780 --> 00:41:03,540
用了各种手段来审视宇宙
have very different ways of looking at the Universe,

796
00:41:03,650 --> 00:41:06,170
但他们都同意一件事——
but they all agree on one thing --

797
00:41:06,290 --> 00:41:08,640
我们将永远解不开这个谜团
we'll never solve the mystery

798
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:11,510
若是我们不做侦测工作的话
if we don't do the detective work.

799
00:41:11,630 --> 00:41:13,610
斯莫林：你得倍加努力工作
You have to work really hard,

800
00:41:13,730 --> 00:41:16,780
你得准备一个又一个失败
and you have to be prepared to fail over and over again

801
00:41:16,900 --> 00:41:19,320
一个又一个失误
and to make mistakes over and over again.

802
00:41:19,430 --> 00:41:21,520
然而我认为聪明才智也适用于
But I think that that wisdom also applies

803
00:41:21,630 --> 00:41:23,490
整个科学界
to the whole community of science.

804
00:41:23,600 --> 00:41:27,590
也就是说 我们得实验每一个愚蠢错误的想法
That is,we have to experiment with every stupid,wrong idea

805
00:41:27,710 --> 00:41:30,100
然后才能得到正确的概念
before we get onto the right one.

806
00:41:30,210 --> 00:41:33,800
时间或许是现实
Time may be real

807
00:41:33,910 --> 00:41:36,840
或许是假象
or it may be an illusion.

808
00:41:36,950 --> 00:41:39,340
但从我们的角度出发
But from our perspective,

809
00:41:39,450 --> 00:41:41,510
过去已一去不复返
the past is gone forever,

810
00:41:41,620 --> 00:41:44,280
未来还尚未写就
and the future is yet to be written.

811
00:41:44,390 --> 00:41:46,210
不管我们能否发现
Whether or not we discover

812
00:41:46,330 --> 00:41:50,120
我们无法感知的时间的物理模样
there are physical aspects of time we can't perceive,

813
00:41:50,230 --> 00:41:51,820
我们人类所体验的
our human experience

814
00:41:51,930 --> 00:41:55,260
生死无尽循环将不会改变
of the endless cycle of life and death won't change.

815
00:41:55,370 --> 00:41:58,260
我童年的金色夏天
The golden summers of my childhood

816
00:41:58,370 --> 00:42:00,400
已一去不复返了
are gone forever.

817
00:42:00,510 --> 00:42:04,000
但是新的夏天就在前头——
But there are new summers ahead --

818
00:42:04,110 --> 00:42:09,350
充满着诱惑的夏天尚未到来
summers rich with the potential of things yet to come.

819
00:42:12,520 --> 00:42:14,520
-- 感谢观赏 --

